{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1453442-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea-but-on-dry-land","id":1453442,"title":"[They Came From Beneath the Sea] ...but on dry land","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","They Came From...","...Beneath the Sea!"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-25T05:45:58-07:00","id":1453442,"title":"[They Came From Beneath the Sea] ...but on dry land","content":"I am very tempted to take advantage of the current DriveThruRPG premium book sale to pick up They Came From Beneath the Sea. I am interested in the 1950s sci-fi genre it is indulging in, but I am specifically interested in the desert-based setting of the classic Them! (or the old video game It Came From The Desert).<br /> How much work would be involved in divorcing the game from it's watery default setting? Is is simply a reskinning of some enemies, or are there lots of character options relating to the sea that would need to be altered also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3580-monkeybloke","name":"MonkeyBloke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T05:55:16-07:00","id":1453444,"title":"","content":"You'll be fine from the player character side of things. Where you'll need to do some work is the antagonist side of things. Pretty much all the monsters in the book are water-themed. You should be able to do some re-skinning, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T09:25:53-07:00","id":1453459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkeyBloke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1453442-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea-but-on-dry-land#post1453442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very tempted to take advantage of the current DriveThruRPG premium book sale to pick up They Came From Beneath the Sea. I am interested in the 1950s sci-fi genre it is indulging in, but I am specifically interested in the desert-based setting of the classic Them! (or the old video game It Came From The Desert).<br /> How much work would be involved in divorcing the game from it's watery default setting? Is is simply a reskinning of some enemies, or are there lots of character options relating to the sea that would need to be altered also?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned above, the playable options are fine, and the core rules work perfectly well whether at sea, on land, or in space. Plenty of the antagonists are adaptable to land-based threats as well. Just make the gillfolk sandfolk and the werelobster a werescorpion. All very easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T12:46:55-07:00","id":1453473,"title":"","content":"Great to know, thanks for the information both. Knowing that this is pretty easily expandable puts any fears I have to rest. <b>Sold!</b><br /> I now regret missing out on the <i>They Came From Beyond The Grave </i>kickstarter, mostly because <i>They Came From Camp Murder Lake</i> is right in my wheelhouse. I guess I'll look to grab it on release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3580-monkeybloke","name":"MonkeyBloke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T13:00:11-07:00","id":1453474,"title":"","content":"You can pre-order Grave! if you want to here: <a href=\"https://they-came-from-beyond-the-grave.backerkit.com/hosted_preorders\" target=\"_blank\">https://they-came-from-beyond-the-gr...sted_preorders</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T03:55:10-07:00","id":1453532,"title":"","content":"So, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Crw1vWJqJk\" target=\"_blank\">They</a> Came From <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=liJfZvXdiTE\" target=\"_blank\">Beneath</a> the Sand, you say?<br /> No problem, afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T08:29:47-07:00","id":1453557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1453442-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea-but-on-dry-land?p=1453532#post1453532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Crw1vWJqJk\" target=\"_blank\">They</a> Came From <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=liJfZvXdiTE\" target=\"_blank\">Beneath</a> the Sand, you say?<br /> No problem, afaik.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremors is an all-time classic, but I think my direct inspiration came from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IP8Z6yvGnc\" target=\"_blank\">this classic</a> (well, classic to me) video game from my childhood. Funnily enough, while searching for that video I found a recent <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0QQ_8XmGpU4\" target=\"_blank\">film with the same name </a>I'll need to check out.<br /> I am of course aware that game is inspired (very closely) by <i>Them!</i> from 1954, which I see is listed in the inspiration section of They Came From Beneath the Sea, so I guess it's not going to be too much of a stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3580,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3580-monkeybloke","user":"MonkeyBloke","date":". 06-26-2021, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3580-monkeybloke","name":"MonkeyBloke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T11:27:02-07:00","id":1453571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkeyBloke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beneath-the-sea/1453442-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea-but-on-dry-land?p=1453557#post1453557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremors is an all-time classic, but I think my direct inspiration came from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IP8Z6yvGnc\" target=\"_blank\">this classic</a> (well, classic to me) video game from my childhood. Funnily enough, while searching for that video I found a recent <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0QQ_8XmGpU4\" target=\"_blank\">film with the same name </a>I'll need to check out.<br /> I am of course aware that game is inspired (very closely) by <i>Them!</i> from 1954, which I see is listed in the inspiration section of They Came From Beneath the Sea, so I guess it's not going to be too much of a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Room for all in a session - or season - i think. Space for all of them and then some in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XfR9iY5y94s\" target=\"_blank\">the land down under</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T14:41:34-07:00","id":1453593,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think you could very easily do enough stuff about Beneath the Sea set on dry land, especially the desert or scrubland, to make a good sized sourcebook (official or Nexus). Giant ants and Gila monsters, grabboid worms, animated dinosaur fossils, Roswell aliens, were-coyotes, snake people, weird cults, desert kaiju, and so forth. Plus all the appropriate environmental rules, a run down of the various deserts around the globe, and whatever else seems appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"